                'lede' => 'Occupied Poland ran an underground parliament, courts, schools and a press, and the largest resistance army in occupied Europe, the Home Army, in Polish Armia Krajowa. Polish forces also fought everywhere the Allies did, from the Battle of Britain to Monte Cassino.',
