            'uprising' => [
                'index' => '05',
                'label' => 'The Warsaw Uprising',
                'title' => 'Sixty-three days, then the city itself',
                'lede' => 'On 1 August 1944 the Home Army rose against the German occupation, expecting a short fight and Soviet help from across the river. It lasted 63 days. The Red Army stopped on the far bank, and historians still argue how much of that was exhaustion and how much Stalin\'s choice. Warsaw was then demolished on orders, building by building.',
