                'topics' => [
                    [
                        'title' => 'Why August 1944',
                        'note' => 'The Red Army was already at the river, and the Home Army wanted to greet it as the host of Warsaw rather than let Moscow simply take the city.',
                    ],
                    [
                        'title' => 'The fighting and the civilians',
                        'note' => 'Most of the dead were civilians. Estimates of civilian deaths range from about 150,000 to 200,000, and historians still differ.',
                    ],
                    [
                        'title' => 'The destruction that followed',
                        'note' => 'Demolition squads worked through the emptied city until January 1945. Counting 1939 and the ghetto too, estimates put the destruction at around 85 per cent.',
