                'alt' => 'A row of burnt-out tenement facades with empty windows above an open square covered in rubble',
                'caption' => 'The Old Town Market Square in Warsaw in 1945, burnt out and waiting to be rebuilt',
                'credit' => 'Photo: Jan Bulhak, Wikimedia Commons, public domain',
                'topics' => [
                    [
                        'title' => 'Yalta and Potsdam',
                        'note' => 'The United States, Britain and the Soviet Union agreed the borders at Yalta in February 1945 and at Potsdam that summer. No Polish government was there.',
