        'language' => [
            'label' => 'One thing worth getting right',
            'title' => 'German camps in occupied Poland, never "Polish camps"',
            'body' => 'Auschwitz, Treblinka, Sobibor and the rest were built and run by Nazi Germany in a country it had occupied. The phrase "Polish death camps" appears in foreign media by accident several times a year, and it moves the blame onto the people who were also being murdered there. The accurate phrase is "German Nazi camps in occupied Poland".',
