            'label' => 'Where this comes from',
            'body' => 'The figures on the Holocaust in occupied Poland, on Operation Reinhard and on Polish war dead follow the United States Holocaust Memorial Museum. The dates of the September campaign follow the same encyclopedia, and Westerplatte follows the Museum of the Second World War in Gdansk, which calls it the symbolic site of the outbreak. Every casualty figure on this page is an estimate. Where historians differ, the page gives the range instead of picking the tidier number. Background photograph: All Saints Day in a cemetery in Zabrze, by MichalPL, CC0. The seven photographs and documents on this page come from Wikimedia Commons and each one carries its photographer and licence beneath it.',
