                'body' => 'Gniezno stands on a hill above a lake, and the hill mattered long before the country did. From the late 700s a stone mound ten to twelve metres across stood here, ringed by a ditch twelve metres wide, and archaeologists read it as a place of worship. It was destroyed in the 940s, and tree rings put the stronghold that the Polans, the tribe this country is named after, raised on the same ground at exactly those years, 940 and 941. Whatever was believed on this hill, the new state went up on top of it.',
