                'photo' => 'chronicle',
                'label' => 'The first chronicle',
                'year' => 'about 1113',
                'title' => 'The oldest chronicle of Poland has never heard of Lech',
                'body' => 'The first history of Poland was written around 1113 by a foreign monk whose name nobody knows, so he is called Gallus Anonymus. He tells how a wheelwright named Piast replaced a ruler named Popiel, and that is where he says the dynasty began. There is no Lech in it, no three brothers and no eagle. The most famous Polish origin story is missing from the oldest book that set out to tell one.',
                'caption' => 'The opening page of the chronicle of Gallus Anonymus',
