                'photo' => 'bird',
                'label' => 'The nest',
                'year' => 'before 1296',
                'title' => 'Let us build a nest here, and the city keeps the name',
                'body' => 'The line everyone remembers comes from the Greater Poland Chronicle, written before 1296: Lech sees a white eagle over its nest and says to build a nest here. Gniezno really does come from gniazdo, the Polish word for nest, so the chronicler was explaining a name that already existed rather than inventing one. The bird here is a white-tailed eagle, the species usually read into the coat of arms, though the heraldic bird was never drawn from a living one.',
                'caption' => 'A white-tailed eagle, the species usually read into the coat of arms',
