                'body' => 'Between that seal and today the eagle was redrawn in every century, as this plate printed in 1935 shows. The version in force now was designed by the artist Zygmunt Kaminski and adopted on 13 December 1927. After the war the communist authorities took its crown away, because a crown stood for monarchy and for sovereignty, and the constitution of 1952 shows the bird bare-headed. On 9 February 1990 the Sejm, the Polish parliament, voted the crown back. Knowing that, you can date almost any Polish eagle you meet, on a building, a document or a grave.',
                'caption' => 'Twenty Polish eagles from the 12th century to 1927, printed in 1935',
