                'title' => 'A pagan duke, known only from what foreigners wrote',
                'body' => 'In the 960s Mieszko I ruled the Polans, the tribe that gave Poland its name. He is the first of his family, later called the Piasts, recorded in his own lifetime, and he held his land through a ring of earth and timber strongholds like Grzybowo, seen here in a laser scan from the air. His people did not write, so not one word of theirs survives. Everything we know comes from outsiders. Around 965 Ibrahim ibn Yaqub, a Jewish traveller from Muslim Spain, counted Mieszko among the four kings of the Slavs and called his land the largest of their countries. Apart from him, only Saxon churchmen wrote about Mieszko, and mostly when their side was fighting him.',
