        'sources' => [
            'label' => 'Where this comes from',
            'body' => 'Most of what we know about the battle comes from Jan Dlugosz, who wrote his Annals decades later and had the story from his father, a veteran of it. A shorter account, the Cronica conflictus, was written soon after. Army sizes are modern estimates and differ widely. The losses among the Order’s knight-brothers are those given by the Museum of Polish History. Whether the Lithuanian withdrawal was a flight or a feint is still argued. The terms of the agreements of 1343, 1385, 1411 and 1466 come from the documents, which survive. The Banderia Prutenorum is kept in the Jagiellonian Library in Krakow. The mass graves at the chapel were excavated between the 1960s and the 1980s.',
