                'label' => 'Buying peace',
                'year' => '1333 - 1343',
                'title' => 'A king of 22 buys peace instead of fighting for it',
                'body' => 'Lokietek died in March 1333, and on 25 April his son Casimir, aged 22, was crowned on Wawel. He inherited about 106,000 square kilometres, an occupied Kuyavia and two enemies: the Order, and John of Luxembourg, king of Bohemia, who still called himself king of Poland. Casimir paid rather than fought. In 1335 John dropped the title for 20,000 threescore Prague groschen, 1.2 million silver coins, and Casimir gave up Silesia, most of which stayed outside Poland until 1945. In 1343, at Kalisz, the Order handed Kuyavia back and kept Gdansk.',
