                'body' => 'Casimir married four times, twice while his second wife, Adelaide of Hesse, was still alive, once on a papal dispensation that turned out to be forged. He had daughters and a grandson, but no legitimate son. In September 1370 he fell from his horse while hunting near Przedborz, the injured leg brought on a fever, and he died on Wawel on 5 November. Under agreements made decades earlier the crown went to his nephew, Louis, king of Hungary, crowned twelve days later. The Piasts, the dynasty of Mieszko I, never wore the Polish crown again.',
                'caption' => 'Casimir as Jan Matejko drew him for his series of Polish kings, 1890s',
                'credit' => 'Drawing: Jan Matejko, public domain',
