                'body' => 'The rebuilding of Wawel, the royal castle on its hill above the Vistula in Krakow, began in 1504 under an architect from Florence whom Poles call Franciszek Florentczyk, Francis the Florentine. After his death in 1516 another Florentine, Bartolomeo Berrecci, took over, and by 1536 three storeys of arcades ran round the courtyard. In 1518 King Sigismund married Bona Sforza, the daughter of a duke of Milan, who brought Italian courtiers, gardeners and cooks to Krakow. Poles still call soup vegetables wloszczyzna, "Italian things", and credit Bona with bringing them, though that is a story people tell rather than a record.',
