                'label' => 'Polish in print',
                'year' => '1473 - 1580',
                'title' => 'Poles are not geese: the country writes in Polish',
                'body' => 'Printing reached Krakow in 1473, yet for decades most books were in Latin, the language of Church, law and university. In 1513 the Krakow printer Florian Ungler issued Raj duszny, The Paradise of the Soul, a prayer book translated by Biernat of Lublin: the earliest known book printed wholly in Polish, found only in fragments. Mikolaj Rej, a country nobleman and a Calvinist, wrote in Polish, not Latin, and said why in a couplet of 1562: let other nations know that Poles are not geese, and have a language of their own. Jan Kochanowski, secretary to Sigismund Augustus, wrote his Laments after his small daughter Urszula died. Printed in 1580, they are still taught in Polish schools.',
                'caption' => 'The title page of Kochanowski\'s Laments, in the Krakow edition of 1583',
                'credit' => 'Print, Krakow 1583, public domain',
            ],
            [
                'key' => 'augustus',
                'photo' => 'arras',
                'label' => 'The last Jagiellon',
                'year' => '1530 - 1572',
                'title' => 'The last Jagiellon leaves his tapestries to the state',
                'body' => 'Sigismund the Old had his son crowned in 1530, aged nine, and Sigismund Augustus reigned alone from his father\'s death in 1548. He married a Lithuanian noblewoman, Barbara Radziwill, in secret, against the will of the lords and of his mother, Bona. Barbara died in 1551, months after her coronation. Bona went home to Italy in 1556 and died there a year later. The king ordered well over a hundred tapestries from Brussels, and his will of 1571 left them, once his sisters had died, to the Commonwealth, not to future kings. In 1569, at Lublin, he and the Sejm joined Poland and Lithuania into one state, where the next topic begins. He died childless in 1572, the last male Jagiellon.',
                'caption' => 'One of the Brussels tapestries with the monogram SA of Sigismund Augustus, about 1560',
