                'year' => '966 - 1370',
                'title' => 'The Middle Ages sit in two clusters, a train ride apart',
                'body' => 'The early state grew up around Poznan and Gniezno in the west, in the region called Greater Poland. The kingdom of the 1300s was run from Krakow in the south, in Lesser Poland. That gives you two bases, and the fastest trains between them take four to five hours, so give each at least two days. The frames that follow go site by site, and for each one they say what is really medieval, what was rebuilt later and how to get there. Travel times are approximate, and opening hours change with the season, so check with the site before you go.',
