                'label' => 'Poznan',
                'year' => 'from 968',
                'title' => 'Under a rebuilt cathedral, the footings of the first',
                'body' => 'Poznan cathedral stands on Ostrow Tumski, the island where the town began. It burned in February 1945, and what you see above ground was rebuilt in 1946-1956. The Middle Ages are underneath: the stone footings of the first cathedral, built in the second half of the 900s, and two graves the cathedral calls most probably those of Mieszko I and his son Boleslaw. Start at Porta Posnania, a centre across the river that explains the island, then walk to the Genius loci reserve, where the timber ramparts of the 10th-century stronghold lie open under a roof. The gilded chapel with bronze statues of both rulers dates from the 1830s.',
