                'title' => 'An island you can only reach in season, by ferry',
                'body' => 'Between Poznan and Gniezno lies Lake Lednica, and on its island Mieszko I built a stone palace with a chapel. In the chapel are two basins made for baptism, found in 1988-1989, and historians count the island among the places where his own baptism may have happened. Two timber bridges led to it. Tree rings date their piles to 963-964, and at the western end you can still see rows of them in the water. The ferry runs only in season, roughly mid-April to October. The open-air village museum next door, at Dziekanowice, shows farms of the 18th and 19th centuries, not medieval ones.',
                'caption' => 'The stone palace and chapel of Mieszko I on Ostrow Lednicki',
