                'key' => 'wawel',
                'photo' => 'wawel',
                'label' => 'Wawel',
                'year' => '1100s - 1364',
                'title' => 'Under the royal cathedral, a crypt from the 1100s',
                'body' => 'In Krakow the Middle Ages begin on Wawel hill. Beneath the cathedral is the crypt of St Leonard, eight columns under a low vault, the surviving part of the Romanesque cathedral that stood here by 1118. The cathedral above it is Gothic, begun in 1320 and consecrated in 1364 with Casimir the Great present, and it holds his tomb and that of his father, Lokietek, the first king crowned here. The Lost Wawel exhibition shows a round stone church from around 1000, partly rebuilt in 1917-1918. From the hill it is a short walk to the Main Square, laid out in 1257, and to Kazimierz, the town Casimir founded in 1335.',
                'caption' => 'The Romanesque crypt of St Leonard under Wawel Cathedral',
