            'body' => 'Dates come from the sites themselves: the cathedrals of Poznan and Krakow, the Museum of the First Piasts at Lednica, the Wawel Royal Castle, the Krakow Saltworks Museum in Wieliczka, the Ojcow National Park and the national register of historic monuments. Where a claim rests on interpretation the page says so: the graves under Poznan cathedral are most probably those of Mieszko and Boleslaw, the baptism may or may not have taken place at Lednica, and the remains in Plock are identified by tradition. Travel times and the Wislica closure were checked in September 2026 and can change.',
