                'year' => '1569',
                'title' => 'Two states with one king, one Sejm and one coin',
                'body' => 'On 1 July 1569 the senators and envoys of both countries swore the union, and on 4 July the king confirmed it. The Kingdom of Poland, which Poles called the Crown, and the Grand Duchy of Lithuania became one Commonwealth, Rzeczpospolita in Polish. From then on they would elect one king together, crown him in Krakow, meet in one Sejm, held in Warsaw, run one foreign policy and strike coins of the same weight. Each kept its own offices, treasury, army and law, and the lands moved to the Crown kept their Lithuanian law too. The Crown sent more envoys to the Sejm and became the stronger partner.',
                'caption' => 'The act of the Union of Lublin, 1 July 1569, with the seals of those who swore it',
