                'photo' => 'confederation',
                'label' => 'Peace between faiths',
                'year' => '1572 - 1573',
                'title' => 'No king, and a promise not to kill over faith',
                'body' => 'Sigismund Augustus died on 7 July 1572, with no heir at all. Until a new king was chosen, the head of the Polish Church, Archbishop Jakub Uchanski, stood in as interrex. That August, in Paris, Catholics killed thousands of Protestants in the St Bartholomew\'s Day massacre. On 28 January 1573 the nobles meeting in Warsaw swore that they, dissidentes de religione, divided in religion, would keep the peace and shed no blood over faith. It was a promise among nobles. The same act kept every lord\'s power over his subjects, in spiritual matters too, so it gave peasants no freedom of their own. Of the bishops, only Franciszek Krasinski of Krakow sealed it.',
                'caption' => 'The act of the Warsaw Confederation, 28 January 1573, with its wax seals',
