            [
                'key' => 'today',
                'photo' => 'chapel',
                'label' => 'Where to see it',
                'year' => 'today',
                'title' => 'A chapel, a synagogue and two mosques',
                'body' => 'Start in Lublin. The castle museum shows Jan Matejko\'s painting of the union, and next to it is the Holy Trinity Chapel, a Gothic chapel that Jagiello had Ruthenian painters cover in Byzantine-style frescoes, finished in 1418. In Krakow\'s Kazimierz the Remuh synagogue is still used for prayer, and next door visitors leave notes of prayer on the grave of Moses Isserles. The church at Radruz, on the Ukrainian border, belongs to a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Zamoyski\'s Zamosc, built from 1580, still has its Armenian houses on the market square. East of Bialystok, Tatar families pray in the wooden mosques of Kruszyniany and Bohoniki.',
                'caption' => 'The Holy Trinity Chapel at Lublin castle, painted by Ruthenian artists by 1418',
                'credit' => 'Photo: Grazyna Adamczyk, CC BY-SA 4.0',
            ],
