            'label' => 'Where this comes from',
            'body' => 'The acts of the Union of Lublin and of the Warsaw Confederation survive as sealed parchments in the Central Archives of Historical Records in Warsaw. The Confederation act has been on UNESCO\'s Memory of the World register since 2003. The dates of the Lublin Sejm follow the State Archive in Lublin and the Museum of Polish History. The account of Jewish life follows the POLIN Museum of the History of Polish Jews. The phrase about a paradise comes from an anonymous lampoon written as an attack. That the Karaites came to Trakai with Vytautas is their own tradition. Matejko\'s painting is a work of 1869, not a record of 1569. Title picture: Waclaw Grodecki\'s map of Poland and Lithuania in Abraham Ortelius\'s atlas of 1570, public domain.',
