                'body' => 'In 1648 the Cossacks, free soldiers of the steppe, rose under Bohdan Khmelnytsky and beat the Crown\'s armies. In 1654 he took the Tsar of Muscovy as overlord, and Muscovy invaded. In 1655 Charles X Gustav of Sweden invaded too, and many nobles swore loyalty to him, a young officer named Jan Sobieski among them. The monastery of Jasna Gora at Czestochowa held out against a Swedish siege. King John Casimir, a son of Sigismund III, won the nobles back, and by 1660 the Swedes had gone. Poles call the Swedish war the Deluge. By the truce of Andrusovo in 1667 Muscovy kept Kyiv and everything east of the Dnieper.',
