                'body' => 'John Casimir gave up the throne in 1668, and the nobles elected Michal Korybut Wisniowiecki, son of a great lord from the borderlands. In 1672 the Ottoman Empire, the Turkish state that ruled the Balkans and much of Hungary, took the fortress of Kamianets in Podolia, and at Buczacz the king\'s envoys agreed to pay it tribute. Sobieski, now grand hetman, commander of the Crown\'s army, refused to accept it. On 11 November 1673 he stormed the Ottoman camp at Khotyn on the Dniester. King Michal had died the day before. In May 1674 the nobles elected Sobieski king as Jan III.',
