                'body' => 'Hungary was split between the Ottomans and Leopold I, the Habsburg emperor in Vienna. In 1682 Hungarian nobles in revolt against Leopold put themselves under Sultan Mehmed IV, and the sultan\'s chief minister, the grand vizier Kara Mustafa Pasha, prepared a campaign against the emperor. France, Leopold\'s great rival, wanted Poland to stay out, but Sobieski wanted Kamianets back and could not take it alone. On 31 March 1683 he allied with Leopold, in a treaty reportedly dated a day early to avoid April Fools\' Day. Each promised help if Krakow or Vienna were besieged.',
                'caption' => 'Kara Mustafa Pasha, grand vizier from 1676, in a portrait painted after his death',
