                'body' => 'Sobieski left Krakow on 15 August 1683. At Tarnowskie Gory, just across the border in Silesia, he said goodbye to Marysienka, his French-born wife Marie Casimire, and rode on with their eldest son, Jakub. His army, over 20,000 strong, marched through Silesia and Moravia, Habsburg lands, to join the imperial army of Charles of Lorraine, Leopold\'s brother-in-law, and the troops of two German electors, Max Emanuel of Bavaria and John George III of Saxony. Some 65,000 to 70,000 men crossed the Danube at Tulln under the overall command of Sobieski, the only king present. By 11 September they stood on the Kahlenberg hills.',
