            'body' => 'The Polish side follows the Museum of King Jan III\'s Palace at Wilanow, which publishes the treaty of 1683, the letters and the march in detail, and the Museum of Polish History. The siege follows the Wien Geschichte Wiki of the City of Vienna, which also records that the hill called the Kahlenberg in 1683 is today\'s Leopoldsberg. Army sizes are contemporary estimates and the sources disagree, so the page gives ranges. The quotations come from Sobieski\'s letter to his wife of 13 September 1683. That the Wawel tents came from Vienna is, for most of them, tradition. Title picture: Folbert van Alten-Allen\'s bird\'s-eye view of Vienna as it stood around 1683, published in 1686, public domain.',
