                'body' => 'Poland\'s open-air museums, called skansens, have moved old village buildings onto one site, and they are the best place to stand in a serf\'s world. The oldest, at Wdzydze Kiszewskie in Kashubia, began in 1906 with one 18th-century hut. At Sanok, in the south-east, some 150 buildings include a manor house beside the cottages. At Kolbuszowa you can walk from a manor house of 1753 to a manor granary of 1784 and the tavern. Maurzyce, near Lowicz, keeps a village laid out round its green. And along the roads of old Galicia, crosses from 1848 still stand.',
