                'body' => 'The first election, in 1573 at the village of Kamien near Warsaw, is told on the faiths page. From 1575 the nobles met on a field at Wola, then a village west of the city. The senators sat in a wooden shed. Everyone else stood in the open, grouped by province under their banners, inside a ditch and a rampart. The primate, the archbishop of Gniezno, who stood in for the king between reigns, went from banner to banner collecting the votes. Every new king swore the Henrician Articles of 1573 and his own list of promises, the pacta conventa.',
