                'body' => 'The Bar Confederation, the nobles\' war against Russia and the king, ended in defeat in 1772. On 5 August, in St Petersburg, Russia, Prussia and Austria signed treaties taking about a third of the Commonwealth\'s land and some four and a half million of its people. A Sejm in Warsaw, with foreign troops in the country, ratified them in September 1773. The partitions era tells that story. Stanislaw August, the king elected in 1764, drew a plain lesson: a state that could not raise taxes or an army would be cut up again.',
