        'sources' => [
            'label' => 'Where this comes from',
            'body' => 'The Great Sejm follows Dzieje Sejmu, the history site of the Chancellery of the Sejm, and the online exhibition of the Central Archives of Historical Records, AGAD, which keeps the original manuscript and gives the count of 182 members, 110 for and 72 against. The day itself and Suchorzewski follow the Museum of King Jan III\'s Palace at Wilanow and the Royal Castle in Warsaw. The articles are quoted from the act. The partition and the Temple of Divine Providence follow the Museum of Polish History, the holiday the Senate of Poland and dzieje.pl. Numbers of troops are the sources\' estimates. Title picture: Jan Matejko\'s Constitution of 3 May 1791, painted in 1891, Royal Castle in Warsaw, public domain.',
