        'sources' => [
            'label' => 'Where this comes from',
            'body' => 'The dates of Kosciuszko\'s life follow the chronology published by the Kosciuszko Mound Committee in Krakow, checked against the Museum of Polish History and the US National Park Service, which runs his house in Philadelphia. The rising follows the Museum of Polish History and dzieje.pl. The hangings follow Rzeczpospolita, Wprost and Polish Radio. Praga follows the Museum of Polish History, the Wilanow Palace Museum and Sztetl on Berek Joselewicz. Numbers of troops and of the dead are estimates and are given as the sources give them. The will follows the Jefferson papers at Founders Online and the US National Archives. Title picture: Kosciuszko in London, painted by Benjamin West in 1797, Allen Memorial Art Museum, Oberlin, public domain.',
