        'sources' => [
            'label' => 'Where this comes from',
            'body' => 'The treaties, the abdication and the convention of 1797 follow the Museum of Polish History and dzieje.pl, checked against the chronology of the Kosciuszko Mound Committee in Krakow and the life of the king published by the Lazienki Royal Museum. The handover of Warsaw follows the Wilanow Palace Museum, that of Krakow the Dzieje Krakowa site. The prisoners follow the Polish Information Agency, Polish Radio and dzieje.pl. The king\'s three graves follow the Museum of Polish History and Polish Radio. The legions follow the Museum of Polish History and dzieje.pl, the song and the anthem the Museum of the National Anthem in Bedomin, a branch of the National Museum in Gdansk. The shares are described, not measured, because the estimates of their size differ. Title picture: William Faden\'s map of the divided Kingdom of Poland, London, 1799, public domain.',
