        'sources' => [
            'label' => 'Where this comes from',
            'body' => 'The duchy, the kingdom and its constitution follow the Museum of Polish History, Britannica and the records of the Sejm held by the Central Archives of Historical Records. The November Night and the war of 1831 follow the Museum of Polish History, dzieje.pl and Polish Radio. The emigration and the repression the Polish Ministry of Education\'s history platform and the Fryderyk Chopin Institute. The Citadel the National Heritage Board and the Museum of Independence. The events of 1861-1864, the counts of clashes, executions and deportations and the historians\' debate follow the Museum of Polish History\'s site on the January Uprising, the Institute of National Remembrance and the National Centre for Culture. Kalinowski follows dzieje.pl, Polish Radio and Lithuanian public radio. Where the sources give different numbers, the page gives a range. Title picture: Polonia 1863 by Jan Matejko, painted in 1864, National Museum in Krakow, public domain.',
