            'body_1' => 'If you see one city in the north of Poland, see this one. The old town looks medieval and most of it is seventy years old: the city was flattened in 1945 and put back up from photographs, paintings and measured drawings. That single fact changes what you are looking at.',
            'body_2' => 'It has been a Teutonic city, a Polish one, a Prussian one, a free city of its own and Polish again. Its people changed with its borders. That is why the question of whether Gdansk is Polish or German has no answer worth giving: it has been both, and for twenty years it was neither.',
