                ['tag' => 'A modern invention', 'title' => 'The trumpeter shot in the throat', 'note' => 'The bugle call from the tower really does break off mid-phrase, every hour. The story that a Tatar arrow hit the trumpeter was made up on the spot in 1925 by a guide, Aniela Pruszynska, answering an American writer, Eric Kelly, who put it in a book in 1928. No earlier source knows it.'],
