            'body' => 'The figure of 799 inhabitants comes from the count of 1820, the year the town was designated for textiles. The ghetto dates are 30 April 1940, when it was sealed, and August 1944, when it was liquidated, and the deportation figures are the ones published by the Auschwitz Memorial and the Marek Edelman Dialogue Centre in Lodz. The film school opened on 8 March 1948. Opening hours and prices are left out on purpose, because they age faster than this page is updated.',
