                ['year' => '1280', 'note' => 'Torun joins the Hanseatic league. For the next two centuries it lives off grain and timber going downriver to Gdansk and the sea.'],
                ['year' => '1454', 'note' => 'The townspeople rise against the Teutonic Order, take the castle and demolish it. They never rebuild it, and the ruin is still there.'],
                ['year' => '1466', 'note' => 'The Second Peace of Torun ends thirteen years of war. The Order gives up the lower Vistula, Gdansk and Malbork to the Polish king, and what is left of it becomes a Polish fief.'],
                ['year' => '1473', 'note' => 'Nicolaus Copernicus is born in a merchant house on Saint Anne Street, now Copernicus Street. He leaves at eighteen and never lives here again, which has not stopped the city from naming everything after him.'],
                ['year' => '1793', 'note' => 'Prussia takes the town in the second partition. It stays German until 1920, when it returns to Poland under the Treaty of Versailles.'],
