                ['tag' => 'Unsettled, and touchy', 'title' => 'Copernicus was Polish', 'note' => 'He was born in 1473 in a town that was under the Polish crown, in a German-speaking merchant family, and he wrote in Latin. Polish and German historians have argued about his nationality for two centuries, which mostly tells you about the 19th century rather than the 15th. The safe and accurate statement is that he was born here, studied at Krakow, and served a bishop in Warmia.'],
