        'sources' => [
            'label' => 'Where this comes from',
            'body' => 'Brine was worked here from the neolithic and rock salt was reached in the second half of the 13th century. Przemysl II chartered the town in 1290 and Casimir the Great issued the statute of the Krakow Saltworks in 1368. The Danilowicz shaft was dug in the 1630s. The chapel of Saint Kinga was begun by the miner Jozef Markowski in 1896 and carried on by Tomasz Markowski and Antoni Wyrodek. Wieliczka was inscribed on the first UNESCO World Heritage list in 1978 and commercial mining ended in 1996. The figures for depth, gallery length and temperature come from the mine itself. Opening hours, ticket rules and prices are left out on purpose, because they age faster than this page is updated.',
        ],

