                    'note' => 'A zapiekanka is half a baguette baked with mushrooms and cheese and finished with ketchup, and it belongs to the 1970s. The round market hall at Plac Nowy in Krakow sells them at three in the morning, which is when they make the most sense. Kebab shops are everywhere and are often very good.',
                    'credit' => 'Photo: Artur Nowacki, CC BY-SA 2.0',
